WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
ii koto arimasu you ni ii koto arimasu you ni

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
kyou mo shan shan shan issho ni

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
shan shan shan waraou

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
honto no onegaigoto wa kossori hiikishite kureru

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
tsuitenai na tte hi no ato wa umeawase shite kureru ne

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
chiccha na koro kara kitto minna shitteru

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
sokkenai furi shinagara itsudemo tsuyoi mikata

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
kamisama wa kyou mo taihen hottokenai shoubun oisogashii

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
ai de minna no genki wo sotto hitonade

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
kamisama to itsumo issho ni yukai ni naru otetsudai

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
daiji na egao mamorou kokoroatari aru desho

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
shan shan moude tokidoki ikanakucha

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.730
Here's page 23.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.750
Page 24, apply the whites.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.150
Next, page 25.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.620
Page 26, redraw these backgrounds more carefully!

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.110
All right, we have one hour until the deadline!

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.980
Let's finish up the last four pages!

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.070
Yukina's Assistants...?

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.580
Editor in Charge
Shinozaki Akane

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.680
We're done!

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.390
Good work!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.260
That was pretty intense.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.420
Yeah, the deadline was earlier than normal.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.850
We're thinking about going out for
a drink. Care to join us, Senpai?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.590
Right now? You guys are so enthusiastic!

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.590
Yukina-sensei, thank you for the manuscript.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.320
All right, I'm going to return to the editorial office for now.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.570
Now...

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.580
please get the manuscript for the special issue done!

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.180
Um, Yukina-sensei?

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.710
What was the editor talking about just then?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.340
Something about a "special issue"?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.310
Didn't I tell you?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.620
N-No way.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:09.540
Starting right now, we'll be working
non-stop to get 40 new pages done!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:04.430
Five days until the deadline!

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:19.190
Deadline Desperation

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.680
Whoa, Kyouko, you sure come up with some crazy ideas.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.880
You're mistaking death gods for hitmen.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.940
We death gods never mess with the living.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.390
We only seek to guide those souls still
attached to the Earth after their death.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.800
So you do
use that, huh?

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.470
The traditional death gods use this to guide them,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.350
but most prefer to use this nowadays.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.660
There's this item too, which will take care of even the most persistent grease stains!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.810
Does that mean we've been living
here with that dangerous thing?!

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.040
Go and hand it over to the SDF or whatever right now!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.530
Th-That's unreasonable!

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.430
Whatever! Hurry up and give me that; it's dangerous!

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.120
Your hysteria is a lot more dangerous, Kyouko!

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:01.890
Oh...

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.340
It seems something has popped out
of the grenade as it rolled away.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.420
A-A safety pin?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.170
T-Take cover!

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:10.550
Blast

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:15.790
Cough

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.790
Man, I'm amazed we're both still alive.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.390
Do something about this right now.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.150
Huh?

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.930
I'm telling you to put everything back together this instant!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.930
You're a death god that completely defies all logic and reason;

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.810
you've got to be able to perform some
miracle or use magic or something!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.660
That's totally out of my league.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.120
Hey, cheer up.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.590
Weep, weep.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.390
How am I going to explain this to my parents?

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.440
Oh...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.930
Magic... magic, huh?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.930
Magical, magical!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:58.020
Whatever, I don't care anymore! Sparkle, sparkle!

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:01.360
A few days later...

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.810
Karin's boss personally came over to apologize and agreed that

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.400
Dokurobei-sama?!

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:10.230
the company would pay compensation for the damaged property.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:10.600
Ding dong

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.560
Oh, someone's here.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.600
I bet it's a newspaper salesman or something.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.670
Yeah, yeah, I'm coming.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.540
Let me pray for you.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.750
Oh! That voice is...

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.110
To be continued

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.240
The story cut off at a really good part this issue.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:37.370
Takita

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:37.370
Bookstore

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.050
I really want to read the next chapter.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.790
Yukina, I came over to play!

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.440
H-Huh? This is strange.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:59.920
Yukina should have finished her
manuscript already and be slacking off.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.240
Oh, it's you, Shamo.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.960
I-I dropped by to play, Yukina!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.500
The situation is desperate; Shamo will do.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.290
This is bad! I have a really bad feeling about this!

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:22.250
Shamo, you're here to read the
manuscript I just finished, aren't you?

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.340
Look! I have a copy of this
month's manuscript right here!

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:29.630
Th-Thanks, but you look busy, so I'll come back later—

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:32.770
Oh, don't mind me, come in and relax.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:36.850
You can stay here for the whole week!

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:39.870
I-I have urgent business to take care of!

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:40.980
You can't escape!

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:44.870
A barrier?!

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:49.180
Yukina, you've got some nerve trapping the Goddess of Poverty.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:53.570
I can easily make your manga not sell a single volume!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:59.720
TL Note: Onmyouji are Japanese mystics that can summon familiars (known as shikigami) to do their bidding.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.460
Don't underestimate an onmyouji.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:59.720
I'll dedicate a luxurious shrine to you and turn you into the goddess of fortune!

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.050
I-I don't want that.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:05.140
Where did all your shikigami go?

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:06.600
Damn them!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:09.130
They all ran away.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.540
At this rate, my manuscript...

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.000
won't make it.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:18.480
You say your shikigami ran away, but you can just take out their contract bond.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.030
I <i>can</i> do that, but...

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:26.250
Shikigami are familiars that have formed a
contract bond with an onmyouji to serve them.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.060
If their master takes out the contract bond, they cannot defy them.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.960
I don't want to use it if at all possible.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.480
Please! Help me out!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.810
I won't make the deadline at this rate!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.680
I understand; I'll give you a hand.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:44.790
So...

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:50.170
Why are you getting us involved?
Helping out a goddess of poverty is just—

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.420
Call me Shamo-san, you stupid cat!

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.360
Y-Yes, Shamo-san.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.860
If I'm going to Hell, you all are coming with me.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.860
We're coming in!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.100
I see, so this is the home of a popular mangaka.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.690
I'm quite thrilled I'm getting to help
someone I admire like Yukina-sensei.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.780
This is unbelievably frugal for a young woman living alone.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.940
You are so rude.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.440
I only tagged along because I was worried about Yuzu-san.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.450
I'm glad you all came!

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.510
I'll pay you for the part-time work, so please do your best!

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:25.580
O-Okay.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:29.030
So what should we do?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.170
You're Yuzu-chan, right?

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:34.100
Hm, let me see.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:35.960
Yeah, you can go make some food for now.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.280
You're probably good at cooking, judging
by your looks, so cook something.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.470
S-Sure.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.550
You can clean up the laundry we
haven't done for the past few days.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.330
You look like a diligent girl.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.480
Yes ma'am!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.130
Here! Right here!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.900
What should I do, Yukina-sensei?

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:58.860
Yoshino, you look like you're very motivated, so help me out along with Shamo.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.100
Wow! That's awesome!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.630
Oh well.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.380
As for you... let's see.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.890
Take care of the background of page 12, the
mob on page 14, and the effects for page 15!

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.300
Why am I the only one getting specific orders?

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:15.040
You look like you can handle it fine.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.960
You can tell from my looks?!

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.010
Though I can definitely do it.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.260
You can?!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.750
So, how should I help out?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.680
Oh, Meiko-chan!

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:24.900
Let's see...

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.780
You look rude but quite spirited;

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:32.010
here's the shopping list and some money!
Go buy some groceries for now.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.470
Wh-Why?!

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.770
Why do I have to go grocery shopping?!

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.930
Then what should I be doing?

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:44.920
Oh, you're a cat god without much divine power, huh?

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.230
Just loaf around.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:51.000
I know I'm in trouble, but I'm not
getting a helping hand from a cat.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.050
S-Sasana is a cat god too!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.910
You just <i>look</i>  useless!

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.880
Shamo, please apply the whites to this page.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.410
Got it.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.420
Sensei, I'm done erasing the initial sketches!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.980
What's up with her? I came all the way to help.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.300
Yoshino-chan, can you dry the ink on this page?

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.920
There's a dryer on the shelf over there.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:11.730
Okay!

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.820
I'm sure I can be more helpful than Yoshino!

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.410
Um, excuse me, Mayu-sama.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:22.650
What is it, Yoshino? Do you need help with something?

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.940
No. You're kind of...

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.690
in the way.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.580
In the way.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.460
Gotta make sure the colors don't mix...

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:42.350
As expected of a grown-up.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:59.200
Five days until the deadline!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:03.200
Weep
weep

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:09.110
My goodness, Mayu-sama, all you're doing is loafing around just like at home.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.970
Exactly.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:12.850
Say, Yukina...

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:13.570
Huh?

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:18.420
Is there anything I can help with?
I feel bad not doing anything.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.160
Here, take this.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.430
Go play with this in the corner.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:30.290
Oh, there's a lot newer game console here!

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.100
New model

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.100
Power consumption is

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.180
This looks good.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.600
Ohoho

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:38.030
Now I just need to microwave it.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:38.530
Start

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:40.360
Oh, found it!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.600
I guess I'll gather some material using the computer.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.010
I knew I needed to divide the load into two!

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:57.250
You are tempting me so much!

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.780
I was worried because they're all novices,
but they're actually pretty helpful!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.020
Even though it'll be close, at this
rate the chapter will get finished!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.720
I-I got the energy drinks you asked for!

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:12.060
Oh, thanks!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.200
Click.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.710
What just happened? Where is everybody?

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:23.990
What is happening?

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:33.680
Everyone, calm down! The circuit breaker must be—

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:37.850
Something warm fell on the desk!

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.350
Don't panic! The breaker is on the wall to the right of the front door!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.320
That hurt.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.150
It's over.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:59.320
It's hopeless now.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.770
Mayu-sama?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.710
W-Wait, how is this my fault?

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:13.970
F-Fine! I'll take responsibility!

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:24.800
Congratulations on
Anime Adaptation

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.670
Nekogami Team: Assemble!

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.060
Tofu

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.060
Thick
fried tofu

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.060
Frozen tofu

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.060
Loose
Tofu

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.060
Saito Foods
Soft Tofu

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:33.080
Looks like we're delivering fresh tofu again today, President!

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:35.560
Tofu

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.570
As I said, I no longer hold that title.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:39.060
Itou Tofu

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:39.060
Cotton

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:39.080
Silk and cotton tofu from the Itou tofu store;

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:43.080
thick, thin, and vegetable fried tofu from Tanaka-san's store;

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.110
loose and soft tofu from Saitou-san's store;

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:50.110
and finally soymilk and the all-important
frozen tofu from Suzuki-san's.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.200
It's really a lot of work just delivering food.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.130
Definitely!

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:59.600
By the way, which do you prefer, silken or cotton tofu?

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:02.530
Let me see, probably silken.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.930
A regular automobile has passed.

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.600
Roger. We confirm.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:08.990
It'll approach Trap A soon!

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.430
Tofu

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.950
I remember the boiled tofu dish I had in Kyoto a long time ago—

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:30.840
Reporting in Chief! One vehicle has passed the lookout line and fell into the trap.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.040
I didn't want to get others involved, but we have no choice.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:37.310
Keep your guard up; the Master will come challenge us soon.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:41.970
Yes, sir! But how do you know it'll be soon?

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.570
The deadline is almost here.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.350
Time is almost up.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.350
Did you hear a crash just now?

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.580
It could've been thunder.

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.230
Those are Yukina's shikigami, huh?

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.580
Th-That's amazing! They're like
special ops forces from movies!

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:09.200
Um, Yukina, why are your assistant
shikigami acting like the Green Beret?

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:13.590
Well, we often did ranger training
and stuff between work.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:17.410
It will be quite a hassle to capture them.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:22.750
Come on, they're your shikigami; you can use a command spell with the contract bond.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:28.500
Fine, I'll go about capturing them without the contract bond.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:31.110
If you aren't going to help, stay here, Yukina.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:34.100
The guard is really tight in the front.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.080
Let's be careful and flank them.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.620
That would be too tedious!

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:41.760
I can handle shikigami of this level on my own!

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:42.500
Meiko!

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:47.810
I'll get this one first.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.140
Bring it on!

00:15:57.650 --> 00:16:03.660
Whoa, did Meiko think we were here to fight?

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.270
She's as self-centered as ever.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.980
What will we do, Mayu-sama?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.100
Well, that's perfect diversion.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.440
Yoshino, Sasana, we'll take a detour and capture the main unit!

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:15.360
Hold it, Meiko!

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.530
Wait!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.290
H-Hey, you!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:26.790
R-Reporting in Chief! It appears Daikokuten-sama's
granddaughter has entered the battlefield.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:27.940
What?!

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.800
Tsk, She must've hired reinforcements.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.940
Avoid facing off with her directly.
Lead her to Point B and you fence it off!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.000
R-Roger!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.850
They're as swift as foxes.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.850
But you can't escape if I do this!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.850
I told you to stop it!

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:50.310
Sasana?

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.530
You just assaulted an ally from behind. What are you doing?

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.980
Are you trying to burn down the whole forest?

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.690
Mayu-sama and Yuzu-sama are in here!

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.940
Do you think I would make such a mistake?

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.200
That's exactly why I stopped you!

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:10.000
They fell for it!

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.380
What is this? A pit trap?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.000
If you're going to fall, don't take me with you!

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.060
All right! Bury them up!

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:21.610
Mayu-sama!

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.390
Remember this!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.340
I heard Meiko-san and Sasana-san!

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.430
The enemy might've got them.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:31.800
This is bad. Yuzu-san's going to be in danger.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.440
Okay. I'll become a bait...

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:34.940
for Yuzu-san's sake!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.690
Yuzu-san!

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:43.410
Cherry blossoms at this time of year?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.430
Damn you! What a strange technique!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.790
Beautiful flowers have bloomed.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.420
Secured!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.160
I can't believe my attack didn't work!

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:57.610
Weep, weep!

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:58.680
Yoshino-chan...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.860
That was supposed to be an attack?

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:04.420
Screw them for acting all on their own!

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:06.060
Speaking of which, what happened to Gonta-san?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:09.080
I don't know! I bet he turned tail and ran off!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:13.190
Don't move; you're completely surrounded.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.390
Give up and surrender.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.950
Oh, you seem to be the leader.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.190
And you were hired by Master to be—

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.050
No! I'm doing this of my own accord.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.130
What?

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:31.950
Think about it; does Yukina really need our powers to capture you in the first place?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.710
Th-That's...

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:38.440
She can always force you to obey
her orders using the contract bond.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.960
Yukina isn't using it as a show of good faith.

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:44.470
Then why isn't she here?

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.210
You're an insipid fool.

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.530
Please stop, both of you.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:49.830
M...

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.270
Master!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.060
Look at this.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.850
That's the contract bond!

00:18:55.940 --> 00:19:00.560
It's the end if you take that out.
We shikigami are helpless against it.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:11.080
This nullifies the contract between us.
Feel free to go wherever you want.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.370
I see, I get what you're saying.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:21.000
You don't have any need for shikigami
that don't follow your orders, do you?

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:26.130
Farewell! I never disliked you.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.840
You dimwits!

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:32.460
There may no longer be a subservient relationship between you, but the bond isn't gone!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:38.950
You are invaluable to me.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:45.880
We've made it through Hell and back countless times,
even after wasting hours playing useless survival games.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.340
Yukina.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:49.390
I'm not your master anymore.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:50.980
But...

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.280
if you're still willing,

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:58.080
please lend me your power one more time!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.590
Master.

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.800
Master!

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:14.130
Great!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.260
Oh my.

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:17.010
Come on.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:19.740
You guys are so...

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.750
Don't bite my shoulder.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:25.450
My hair and clothes are all muddy.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.820
It's all your fault!

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.030
What did you say?!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.020
Weep, weep.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.550
Someone!

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:35.030
Yuzu-san!

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.280
We have to deliver the tofu that aren't destroyed!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.060
You're a model deliveryman, President.

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:46.310
I no longer hold that title though.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:49.390
No, you're still the President, President!

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:52.620
Takita

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:52.620
Bookstore

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.320
Yuzu, look at this!

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:55.380
This has the manga from last time!

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.620
Oh, you're right!

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:02.450
I was worried how it would end up, but I can feel this is done with even more passion.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:07.600
Since it's in the magazine, she must've
made up with her shikigami.

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.660
I wonder if they got a raise.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.440
Heh, about that...

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.440
she agreed to make homemade pudding as a snack.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:22.950
Yukina-sensei! You can just buy some from the store!

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.380
You're making a lot of money, you know.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:29.890
Pudding! Pudding! Pudding!

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:30.460
I have no choice! They won't be satisfied if it's not my handmade pudding!

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:32.290
Is the pudding ready yet?

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:33.380
I know, I know!

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:39.040
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:38.970
That makes me want to eat Yuzu's homemade pudding.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:42.410
So can you make me some?

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:43.250
Sure.

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:54.380
Oh my, this town has changed completely.

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
yukkuri nozokikonda ashita to iu mirai

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
sakasama ni nagameta sekai

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
kirameku watagashigumo ni omoide wo utsushite

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
nanairo no ribon wo kaketa

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
hitori ni naru to samishikute fukigen yo

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
itsudatte koko ni ite

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
So stay here forever

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
dare ni demo kitto aru wa

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
tojikometa negai no kakera

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:51.660
Baby! Oh My God!

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
kienai chiisana omoi no kagi ni furete hoshii yeah

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
yasashii kioku e to tsuredaseru no wa

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
itsudatte kimi dake

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.940
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:14.810
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:16.590
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:17.520
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.300
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.380
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:30.030
I see a flower in the garden. It must already be summer!

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:31.240
What is it?

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:33.170
It's quite rare to see you space out.

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:36.660
Could it be that Yaoyorozu-dou is
out of funds? Is it my fault?

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:40.540
No, I was reminiscing about my childhood a bit.

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Memory Halation Summer
